    {
      "v": 2,
      "zh": "亚哈谢在撒马利亚，一日从楼上的栏杆里掉下来，就病了；于是差遣使者说：「你们去问以革伦的神巴力．西卜，我这病能好不能好。」",
      "en": "Ahaziah fell through a window lattice in his upper chamber in Samaria[NOTE:1] and was injured. He sent messengers with these orders,[NOTE:2] “Go, ask[NOTE:3] Baal Zebub,[NOTE:4] the god of Ekron, if I will survive this injury.”",
      "notes": [
        "For location see Map2-B1; Map4-D3; Map5-E2; Map6-A4; Map7-C1.",
        "Heb “and he sent messengers and said to them.”",
        "That is, “seek an oracle from.”",
        "Apparently Baal Zebub refers to a local manifestation of the god Baal at the Philistine city of Ekron. The name appears to mean “Lord of the Flies,” but it may be a deliberate scribal change of Baal Zebul, “Baal, the Prince,” a title known from the Ugaritic texts. For further discussion and bibliography, see HALOT 261 s.v. בַּעַל זְבוּב and M. Cogan and H. Tadmor, II Kings (AB), 25."
